## Erlang VM arguments for the Nexus production release.
## This file is an EEx template — <%= ... %> expressions are evaluated at
## release build time by `mix release`.

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------
## Distributed Erlang
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------

## Erlang cluster cookie — must match across all worker nodes (node1, node2).
## Set via environment variable; never hardcode in source control.
-setcookie <%= System.fetch_env!("ERL_COOKIE") %>

## Node failure detection heartbeat.
## A node that misses all ticks for net_ticktime seconds is declared dead.
## 15s: fast enough for production failover, tolerant of transient network
## hiccups and short GC pauses. Default is 60s.
-kernel net_ticktime 15

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------
## Scheduler / SMP
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------

## Enable kernel polling for efficient I/O. Required for high-throughput
## event processing under the Commanded EventStore workload.
+K true

## One scheduler thread per CPU core. BEAM auto-detects the correct count
## from the runtime environment (ECS task CPU units, EC2 vCPUs, etc).
+S <%= System.schedulers_online() %>:<%= System.schedulers_online() %>

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------
## Memory
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------

## Limit the maximum size of a single binary on the binary heap before it
## is moved to the global binary heap. Keeps per-process memory bounded
## when large event payloads (KYB documents, COSE keys) are processed.
+hmax 134217728

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------
## Crash dumps
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------

## Write crash dumps to /tmp so they land on fast ephemeral container
## storage rather than the virtiofs-mounted source volume.
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP /tmp/erl_crash.dump
